    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Data Loader: one card becomes one row\n\n**Input: 1 card (`$json`)** with two separate parts:\n- `content` = legal text\n- `metadata` = 9 labels (gesetz, typ, nummer, titel, fundstelle, quelle, stand, fassung, thema -> thema allows to search more precisely)\n\n**The loader repacks it:**\n- Field *Data* = `{{ $json.content }}` → text, becomes the vector\n- *Options → Metadata* → labels, only attached (not vectorised)\n\n**Output: 1 row in Supabase `documents`, 4 columns:**\n- `id`: running number\n- `content`: legal text\n- `metadata`: all 9 labels as one JSON block\n- `embedding`: 1536 numbers (helper *Embeddings OpenAI*)\n\nNo separate column per label: filter later via `metadata.gesetz` etc.\n\n---\n\n## Text Splitting: Custom instead of Simple\n\n**Problem:** *Simple* cuts every text again into pieces of about 1000 characters (200 overlap). Our cards are already split (article or \"part 1/2\"), on average about 2000 characters, most up to 4000, a single paragraph stays whole up to 9000 (AI Act Art. 5 paragraph 1 has about 8000). The result would be many more rows than cards, with sentences cut in the middle.\n\n**Solution:**\n- *Text Splitting* = **Custom**\n- Connect a **Recursive Character Text Splitter** to the *Text Splitter* input\n- **Chunk Size 10000** (larger than every card, never cuts)\n- **Chunk Overlap 0**\n\n**Check after the run:** exactly **297 rows**\n`select metadata->>'gesetz', count(*) from documents group by 1;` (DSGVO 118, EU AI Act 179)",
        "height": 716,
        "width": 624,
        "color": "#14C288"
      },
      "id": "f1065ebc-b8ef-4b27-bc48-f0ea4a9cd932",
      "name": "Sticky Note Data Loader",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1424,
        0
      ]
    },
